# An X session on Dolly's display: the Xsdl server, twm managing the
# windows, and three of X's own clients in theirs: a clock, eyes that follow
# the pointer and a terminal with a shell, where imgui-x11 starts Dear ImGui's
# example in a window of its own.
FROM /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-system b6c9b3426382d5dbf6d98423159a74c79aaa168ca83a63509e9ebc1bfd02a9c6
INSTALL /v0.1.4/demos/x11/Dollyfile-xorg-server 750cefc7fcee3cbe8f2544ed6586db83f81481aaf3acf55dbde9366d386b93a6
INSTALL /v0.1.4/demos/x11/Dollyfile-twm ba6a65f15562a6b5eeaba3560d1666b5d4f13f5e44b7696f5302e38d7fa99aea
INSTALL /v0.1.4/demos/x11/Dollyfile-xclock f2b78d1525600564d0268c9c7d92c5155ccb0c29671f98826d925d9ae222346a
INSTALL /v0.1.4/demos/x11/Dollyfile-xeyes cbd343691b80e518c1de2dc3a9da33762c81fd7c1717bac4162ebbc0a49c4633
INSTALL /v0.1.4/demos/x11/Dollyfile-xterm 101f9822a6bd46d440db787411711fd6966027e0dc7ff489ea19f546e1304c16
# amy installs packages into the session (tmux, nvim and the rest), with the
